{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_014Mqd4FZ9wkBsZdG8BMr8ve","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was written for **Q19 — Version and roll back agent behavior?**:\n\n**Core insight:** Agent behavior lives in four independently mutable layers — each needing its own versioning and rollback path:\n\n1. **Prompts** (highest change velocity) — stored in a versioned artifact store (LangSmith prompt hub / Git-backed config), loaded by tag at startup. Rolling back = flipping `stable` tag back. **SLA: <2 min, no code deploy.**\n2. **Tool schemas** — versioned alongside prompts; old versions stay registered until agents drain to avoid mid-flight schema mismatches.\n3. **Orchestration code** (LangGraph DAG / ReAct loop) — Docker-image-tagged, blue-green deployed. 5% canary → metrics gate → promote or rollback image. **SLA: <10 min.**\n4. **Model snapshot** — pinned explicitly (e.g. `gpt-4o-2024-11-20`), promoted only after golden-dataset regression passes.\n\n**Canary flow:** shadow-mode interceptors block irreversible tools (email/payment) from double-executing during canary testing. Auto-rollback fires when turn-count or success-rate SLOs breach by >5%.\n\n**Key pitfalls covered:** Only versioning the model (missing prompts/schemas/code), forgetting shadow-mode interceptors for irreversible tools, and citing \"we can roll back\" without committing to concrete SLA targets per layer."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":354,"cache_read_input_tokens":63472,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":354,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f012b630-d443-4b48-8c88-8182aaa6f1cb","uuid":"ac787ea5-0590-4144-8f3d-de552a2fc47e"}
